  "result": "That matches the doc. So I've confirmed exactly two discrepancies between the data dictionary and the schema:\n\n1. **`docs/db/tables-issues.md`** — documents `issues_project_number_idx` as covering `org_id, number`, but `src/server/db/schema/issues.ts:39` declares `uniqueIndex(\"issues_project_number_idx\").on(table.projectId, table.number)` — the actual columns are `project_id, number`, not `org_id, number`. (The doc's own later prose at line 64-65 even correctly says the index is on `(project_id, number)`, contradicting its own index table two sections earlier.)\n\n2. **`docs/db/tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md`** — documents an index `search_index_org_updated_idx` on `org_id, updated_at`, but `src/server/db/schema/webhooks.ts` declares only one index on `search_index` (`search_index_org_kind_idx`, on `org_id, subject_kind`); there is no `updated_at` column on the table at all and no second index.\n\nAll other index descriptions across `docs/db/tables-*.md` were checked against every `index(...)`/`uniqueIndex(...)` declaration in `src/server/db/schema/*.ts` and matched exactly.\n\nANSWER: docs/db/tables-issues.md, docs/db/tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md",
